    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d656">

                <pb facs="0787" n="695" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg695"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/10178</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Curtis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-27T16:00:00-05:48">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 27, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 29, 1.45 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your May 25, 4 p.m. Of the works cited by you, the Legation, has only the 5th
                    edition of Hall, the 1st of Oppenheim, and Moore’s <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Digest</hi> and I am unable to locate anything of real use in the first of
                    these. Please send immediately the editions cited and also Phillipson.</p>
                <pb facs="0788" n="696" xml:id="pg696"/>
                <p>The Honduran Government is little interested in anything except the regularising
                    of its position as to the alleged sequestration of the German lighters at
                        Amapala<anchor n="1" xml:id="d656-f1"/> and the control of the activities of
                    enemy aliens and other suspicious aliens. As to the rest, it is accomplishing
                    its purposes either openly in accordance with the provisions of martial law or
                    surreptitiously, or else it lacks capacity or power to accomplish them.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Curtis</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d656-f1" n="1" xml:id="d656-f1-content">
                <p>For correspondence regarding the German lighters, see <ref
